<title>CHINA: China launches experimental satellite.</title>
<headline>China launches experimental satellite.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China on Sunday successfully launched an experimental satellite using a Long March 2D rocket, the Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The satellite was launched from a base in Jiuquan in the northwestern province of Gansu, Xinhua said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The satellite went smoothly into orbit and all instruments aboard are operating well,&quot; Xinhua said. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>China's space industry has been plagued by setbacks.</p>
<p>The latest was in August when a domestic communications satellite, launched aboard a Long March 3 rocket from the Xichang space centre in southwestern province of Sichuan, failed to reach its proper orbit.</p>
<p>Previous failures had sent insurance premiums for China's satellite launches soaring.</p>
</text>
